--- Deep Copy via Slicing Tester ---
--- Nested lists and dicts are copied, not shared ---
PASS: original list element changed
PASS: copy kept the old list values
PASS: copied list is a different object
PASS: copied dict is a different object
PASS: changing the copy leaves the original alone
--- Deep nesting ---
PASS: three levels deep are independent
PASS: original shows the change
--- Self-referencing structures ---
PASS: list cycle is preserved in the copy
PASS: list cycle copy is not the original
PASS: dict cycle is preserved in the copy
PASS: dict cycle copy is not the original
PASS: list/dict mutual cycle is preserved
--- Other value kinds survive copying ---
PASS: enum member keeps its identity by name
PASS: enum member keeps its value
PASS: enum survives
PASS: type survives
PASS: built-in function still callable
PASS: float survives
PASS: NULL survives
PASS: TRUE survives
PASS: instance copy keeps its field
PASS: instance copy is a different object
PASS: function still callable
PASS: anonymous function still callable
PASS: bound method still callable
PASS: instance copy does not follow the original
--- Slice edge cases ---
PASS: empty slice
PASS: full slice
PASS: tail slice
PASS: string slice
